OL,0,         GFORUM64   GMi 25 Nov F06:22:08
OL,1,T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOpen source SID chip replacement       
OL,4,G8580/6581 emulator that can be executed
OL,5,Gon Bluepill boards and STM32F103       
OL,7,GLicense - GNU General Public License v3
OL,8,G(derived from Bakisha STM32 SID player)
OL,10,GIntroduction                           
OL,12,GProject is heavily inspired by SwinSID 
OL,13,Gand ArmSID project. And is maintained  
OL,14,Gas an open-source alternative to them. 
OL,15,GNow it is even working on a            
OL,16,GSTM32F103C8T6 on an overclocked freq   
OL,17,G128 MHz with 8 MHz crystal. With some  
OL,18,Gerrors in behavior - some              
OL,19,Greadings/writings from CPU are missing.
OL,20,GI'm looking for contributers(I can even
OL,21,Gpay for the work) who will add some    
OL,22,Gassembler                              
OL,24,D]FForum64.de RSS feed            (3/3) 
